# Test Agents and Plugins

This Livebook tests the same Agent as a value and as a live actor. Direct tests
give fast contract feedback. Actor tests verify commit and process behavior.

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)}
])
```

## Define the subject

```elixir
defmodule TestGuide.Counter do
  use Jido.Agent, name: "test_guide_counter"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{count: Zoi.integer() |> Zoi.default(0)})
  end

  routes do
    signal_source "/guides/test"

    route "counter.add" do
      action %{amount: amount},
        name: "test_guide_add",
        schema: Zoi.object(%{amount: Zoi.integer()}),
        context: context do
        {:ok, %{context.agent_state | count: context.agent_state.count + amount}}
      end

      define :add, args: [:amount]
    end
  end
end
```

## Test the direct contract

The direct path does not start processes. Verify the candidate state,
Directives, and unchanged input value.

```elixir
agent = TestGuide.Counter.new!(id: "direct-test")
{:ok, signal} = TestGuide.Counter.add_signal(3)

{:ok, candidate, []} = TestGuide.Counter.cmd(agent, signal)
0 = agent.state.count
3 = candidate.state.count
```

Invalid input must fail before it can produce a candidate.

```elixir
{:ok, invalid_signal} = TestGuide.Counter.add_signal("three")
{:error, %Jido.Action.Error.InvalidInputError{}} =
  TestGuide.Counter.cmd(agent, invalid_signal)
```

## Test the actor boundary

Start a unique Jido instance for each asynchronous test. This prevents registry
and runtime state from crossing test cases.

```elixir
jido = :"test_guide_#{System.unique_integer([:positive])}"
{:ok, jido_pid} = Jido.start_link(name: jido)
{:ok, server} = Jido.start_agent(jido, TestGuide.Counter, id: "live-test")

before = Jido.AgentServer.snapshot(server)
{:ok, committed} = TestGuide.Counter.add(server, 4)
after_commit = Jido.AgentServer.snapshot(server)

0 = before.state_version
1 = after_commit.state_version
4 = committed.state.count
^committed = after_commit.agent
```

Test process ownership and cleanup explicitly when they are part of the
contract.

```elixir
monitor = Process.monitor(server)
:ok = Jido.stop_agent(jido, server)

receive do
  {:DOWN, ^monitor, :process, ^server, _reason} -> :ok
after
  5_000 -> raise "Agent Server did not stop"
end

:ok = Supervisor.stop(jido_pid)
```

## Test Plugins at both boundaries

For a state-only Plugin, test option normalization, state initialization,
Directive validation, and `update_state/3` as ordinary functions. Then run one
Agent Turn to verify that Plugin state commits with domain state.

For a Plugin runtime, start the Agent under a unique Jido instance. Verify its
child specification, startup failure behavior, Directive handling, cleanup, and
restart behavior. Use messages or public inspection functions instead of sleep
calls.

In this repository, `mix examples` runs the executable example suite. Use
`mix test` for the full contract suite.
